                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8db54872-7249-3ce1-91b8-06b2583e5437",
                        "entry_id": "bd70f6de-90a5-3dbf-8953-4c796ab26917",
                        "glosses": [
                            "abstoßend wirkender Schmutz"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "gehoben",
                            "outdated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ea89625-612e-4c89-a480-242fdb4549c0",
                                "sense_id": "8db54872-7249-3ce1-91b8-06b2583e5437",
                                "text": "„Diese‚ und ein Mischmasch anderen Unflats‘ seien zum Glück aus den Apotheken verschwunden.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8bea42a5-99a7-4bab-a3e4-534d3c17f657",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd70f6de-90a5-3dbf-8953-4c796ab26917",
                        "source_sense_id": "8db54872-7249-3ce1-91b8-06b2583e5437",
                        "source_sense_description": "abstoßend wirkender Schmutz",
                        "target_lang_word": "ordure",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ordure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                        "entry_id": "c8decfff-cf78-3a73-ab2c-fd9272ae4ad5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dung, excrement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d2d5a62-f28a-4797-87ce-49247821596f",
                                                "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                                "text": "But there has none employed my Thoughts of late ſo much, as a very nice inquiſition, or inſpection, into the frequent differences we meet with Human Ordure. The World may ſay, perhaps, I had very little to do, and that ſo ſolemn and ſerious a Preface, ill became ſo foul a Subject; but let what will be ſaid, I can't help communicating my Sentiments, but will endeavour to wrap 'em up in as cleanly a manner, as the dirtineſs of the Theme will admit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44dd7156-2c3b-451d-b8a7-7e74d3753906",
                                                "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                                "text": "If a Man throws upon a Woman's body, from the Navel upwards to beneath the Neck, any Spue, or Urine, or Ordure, or Semen, the Magiſtrate ſhall fine him One Hundred and Twenty Puns of Cowries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c49b8cb-bd84-4d69-b8ef-821122c0d8a6",
                                                "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                                "text": "It seems at first sight a strange thing that Paris, with its apparently pure air, should be by no means so healthy a place to live in as London. [...] Another cause, not so sensible to the eye as to another organ, we have long believed to be, the universal accumulation of ordures in pestiferous cess-pools under or near almost every house. [...] The removal of these ordures is periodical, and must take place in the night. [...] From the cleaned-out dwellings the ordures are taken to the greatest laystall in the world, the Boyauteries of Montfaucon, famous for its filth, its carrion, and countless myriads of rats. Thence they are bought up by growers as manure for the land; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77265193-3e46-4874-bd47-19e3048dc0ab",
                                                "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                                "text": "Also, they say that Margaret Samon, Nicholas Alastre, Thomas de Stanley, John Etwall, Richard Etwall, and William, son of Hugh Spicer, block up the common cavern of the aforesaid town on the northern side with ordure, weeds, and cinders, to the serious damage of the whole town aforesaid, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d2d3ad2-c7a2-4630-b0f0-be49a3102246",
                                                "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                                "text": "Only Madame herself seeing Jacob out had about her that leer, that lewdness, that quake of the surface (visible in the eyes chiefly), which threatens to spill the whole bag of ordure, with difficulty held together, over the pavement. In short, something was wrong."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c60dfc30-395e-4ecf-8d3c-ca776d7259b6",
                                                "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                                "text": "The invention consists in a method of dehydrating animal ordure wherein the ordure is caused to move along a path and subjected to the simultaneous action of a hot air flow, and of ultrasonic and/or microwave radiation during such movement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f15a4662-3897-480e-948f-f62dc2f82fd9",
                                                "sense_id": "078c4948-6fe4-310e-ae8d-ad01512e74d0",
                                                "text": "David Jones had seen death on a vast and public scale but never before domestically and at close quarters. This domestic death revolted him. [...] The bowels and bladder collapsed, sheets and mattress had to be burnt at the bottom of the back garden. The body, having vulgarly shed its ordures, now turned into an ordure itself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b0f6b3b5-9832-3067-861c-ae24eb803909",
                                        "entry_id": "c8decfff-cf78-3a73-ab2c-fd9272ae4ad5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dirt, filth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6756794d-4605-4007-8d23-093e72a3d530",
                                                "sense_id": "b0f6b3b5-9832-3067-861c-ae24eb803909",
                                                "text": "For, that the ordure, which continually gathers on the skin, would ſoon ſtop the pores of it, if the ſweat were not furniſht with ſome efficacious diſſolvent to open and pierce them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20c91a71-7c01-46b7-aa38-0d6fd11cf17e",
                                                "sense_id": "b0f6b3b5-9832-3067-861c-ae24eb803909",
                                                "text": "The Ears are ſometimes troubled with Ulcers; and an Ulcer often happens by the Fall of a malignant Humour; or elſe it is occaſioned by a Wound, ſome Hurt, or ſome Ordure that is corrupted in the Ear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3853a297-d542-33b3-8dc7-9997abd16ece",
                                        "entry_id": "c8decfff-cf78-3a73-ab2c-fd9272ae4ad5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something regarded as contaminating or perverting the morals; obscene material."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1b702e3-19a9-493d-9fa8-f970803a0e43",
                                                "sense_id": "3853a297-d542-33b3-8dc7-9997abd16ece",
                                                "text": "As my Papers are intended for ſhort Eſſays of Morality,—I ſhall leave to the Authors of Common-Senſe, the full Poſſeſſion of their Puns and Ordures, both now and evermore; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0016e431-20fe-4c97-861a-00c517d0b2df",
                                                "sense_id": "3853a297-d542-33b3-8dc7-9997abd16ece",
                                                "text": "[James] Douglas – who had recently railed against Aldous Huxley’s Antic Hay for its ‘ordure and blasphemy’, summed the book [Aleister Crowley’s Diary of a Drug Fiend (1922)] up as ‘describing the orgies of vice practised by a group of moral degenerates who stimulate their degraded lusts by doses of cocaine and heroin’."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3173a37e-f914-4605-8523-043385dcc071",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd70f6de-90a5-3dbf-8953-4c796ab26917",
                        "source_sense_id": "8db54872-7249-3ce1-91b8-06b2583e5437",
                        "source_sense_description": "abstoßend wirkender Schmutz",
                        "target_lang_word": "fumier",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fumier",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96aff2bf-dda9-30b8-858d-23f5f738a166",
                                        "entry_id": "50ab118e-86fd-336c-9288-765cde628c85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mélange des litières (paille, foin, etc.) et des déjections liquides et solides des chevaux et autres animaux d’élevage, décomposé par la fermentation sous l’action de micro-organismes, et utilisé comme engrais et amendement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Élevage"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85c57850-9969-4dc7-bc63-bcc13aa28be4",
                                                "sense_id": "96aff2bf-dda9-30b8-858d-23f5f738a166",
                                                "text": "Elle semblait faite pour glisser, en robe blanche, dans des paysages liturgiques […] En réalité, elle trayait les vaches, cette âme, elle crochait le fumier dans la cour, ce rêve."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a9feb7b-e871-44ec-a777-0d82b6a38b3f",
                                                "sense_id": "96aff2bf-dda9-30b8-858d-23f5f738a166",
                                                "text": "Il avait réussi à prendre quelques photos : des CRS à moitié endormis, bottés et casqués, le Mauser lance-grenades à la bretelle, rencognés, non loin du CHU et de la fac de droit, comme une poignée d’oiseaux mouillés, sous les grimaces provocatrices et vengeresses des masques de pierre du vieil hôtel de Cerisy ; un garde-mobile ronflant la bouche ouverte, le visage grotesquement déformé par la vitre du car Berliet le long duquel sa joue s’était ventousée comme une limace ; un gradé en civil, arrogant et sec, juché sur le refuge central du carrefour des Palomières comme un coq sur son fumier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7410638-b348-450c-a7cd-bf2c8f4d5e63",
                                                "sense_id": "96aff2bf-dda9-30b8-858d-23f5f738a166",
                                                "text": "À condition de cuber l’épandeur en multipliant la longueur par la largeur et par la hauteur du chargement pour connaître le volume de fumier qu’il contient, il est possible d’approcher le poids de fumier chargé de 2 façons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5ca4f31-00d3-4f8c-bba3-545bb8dfe232",
                                                "sense_id": "96aff2bf-dda9-30b8-858d-23f5f738a166",
                                                "text": "Les producteurs n'utilisent aucun produit chimique et emploient comme engrais du fumier, de l’écalure de café et du tourteau de ricin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8333dc7-78f9-36ac-a8c5-587ba7ff33bf",
                                        "entry_id": "50ab118e-86fd-336c-9288-765cde628c85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fumière ; tas de fumier que l’on trouvait dans les cours de ferme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f59855f0-d82f-45b9-aeb0-07ef51986c19",
                                                "sense_id": "c8333dc7-78f9-36ac-a8c5-587ba7ff33bf",
                                                "text": "Il n’y avait dans la cour, formée par quatre pauvres bâtiments, aucun être vivant, sinon les poules picorant le fumier qui, tout près de la bergerie, baignait dans un lit immonde de purin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0860a677-8f3e-35a0-9ec7-96fa017915ca",
                                        "entry_id": "50ab118e-86fd-336c-9288-765cde628c85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personnage odieux."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "offensive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6273b3d1-13b1-4183-baf1-4d258090e575",
                                                "sense_id": "0860a677-8f3e-35a0-9ec7-96fa017915ca",
                                                "text": "Il m'expliqua prolixement, […] ; qu'on ne devait s'attendre à rien d'autre de la part d'un pareil fumier ; que la seule riposte convenable, lui Poirson m’en fichait son billet, c'était, un soir, de s'embusquer au coin d'une rue, d'y guetter Jean-Loup et de « lui faire sa fête »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
